      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "narration_text": "Mechanism one: look before writing. The skill is explicit about this. For a clip, you probe it and inspect representative frames and the event sequence. For a Remotion or Manim scene, you find the existing renderer first, inspect its props and source, then render a small test fixture. For gameplay, you use actual engine capture. Never substitute a fixture, animation, screenshot slideshow, or imagined success.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 24,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "skin_note": "No SkillTeardownMechanism916 — using FormACard916.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "FormACard916",
          "props": {
            "lines": [
              "MECHANISM 1: LOOK BEFORE WRITING",
              "Clip: probe it, inspect frames, keep timecodes.",
              "Scene: find the renderer with ./art scenes,",
              "inspect props, render a test fixture.",
              "Gameplay: use actual engine capture.",
              "Never substitute an imagined success.",
              "—",
              "\"A frame can show a state; it cannot",
              "establish response time, motion,",
              "or causality.\""
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
